after #261 2026-09-09 — #261 N4: the nav label crop was cascade-dead, and the selected row gives back the grey

Dave, verbatim: "the subagents need to be much more careful with the line-height cropping
CSS pattern we have for labels, remove the background grey on the selected state".

THE CROP. The repo's pattern is native leading-trim (canon.css:945-966) plus the truncating-
label exception (`text-box-edge:text text`, so the box does not end on the baseline where
overflow:hidden then eats g/y/p). All three nav snippets had pasted the DEFAULT without
canon's `:where()` wrapper. A bare `:is(button,a,...,input[type=text],...)` takes the
specificity of its heaviest branch and sat at (0,1,1) - above every one-class override in
the same file - so `.nv-label{text-box-edge:text text}` was written and dead, the label
computed `cap alphabetic`, and the descender of "Payments and transfers" was cut.
The list is now wrapped in `:where()` (zero specificity, identical match, exactly as
canon.css wraps it and for the reason canon.css gives), and the trim is restated beside the
edge on `.nv-label` so the pair reads as one decision. Also `.sn-canvas span` -> `>`: the
specimen greeking rule was matching the real `.sn-product` label and forcing it to 12px.

DRIVEN (Chromium, goto file://, ink from the font's own canvas metrics vs the element's
clientHeight): 3 snippets x 4 themes x 2 modes, 336 .nv-label boxes.
  before  272 clipped, worst descender cut 5.50px, 16px label in an 11px box
  after     0 clipped, worst cut 0.00px, 17px box against 15px of ink
_validate_descender_clip.py agrees: Sidebar-nav 4 cascade-dead overrides -> 0.

THE GREY. The current row's fill is removed from the shared item block on all three
surfaces. It was hover's own signal worn permanently, which left hover nothing of its own
to say. Current is aria-current="page" + the 3px indicator bar (a shape) + a weight step on
the label (400 -> 500); the grey means hover and only hover. Driven: the current row
computes rgba(0,0,0,0) with rgb(219,0,17) 3px inset and label weight 500 in all 8
theme x mode combos. The carrier claim is corrected in three metas and two manifests.

Gates: snippets 137/0, coverage 137/137/0, behaviour OK, gen_showroom --check in sync,
hit-area 106 targets / 0 findings --strict, state-contrast 0 fails (Navigations clean;
declared holes only). The two descender reds that remain are not mine - `.demo-grid td` in
Filter-toolbar-bar and `.kpi-lbl` in Kpi-tile, the same bare-`:is()` cause.

Review page re-pointed at ORIGINAL 7647aaf vs #261 N4, N3's type.css bake reapplied to all
six srcdocs, driven across four themes and two modes.
